      "end": 5.00,
      "issue": "The second shot is a closer crop of the boat, not a closer crop inside the existing anchor emphasizing quay, architecture or civilian detail as requested. It introduces a new viewpoint and focuses on an object (the boat) that was not the primary focus of the 'already completed action's resulting state' of the messenger.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "start": 2.30,
      "end": 5.00,
      "issue": "The second shot introduces new characters (people on the boat and on the quay in the background) and removes the messenger from the world, which contradicts the prompt's instruction to 'preserve visible identities, costume colours, existing props and left/right relationships; a closer crop never creates a new person or removes one from the world.'",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "start": 2.30,
      "end": 5.00,
      "issue": "The boat in the second shot is moving, creating a wake, which is an unauthorized action as the prompt stated 'Only the declared small foreground action changes.' and 'Show the already completed action's resulting state; only a tiny eyebrow, cloth or water adjustment already supported by the anchor is allowed.'",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "start": 2.30,
      "end": 5.00,
      "issue": "The lighting and shadows in the second shot appear to shift, particularly on the boat and the buildings, which contradicts the instruction that 'The pictured clear blue sky, golden cloud shapes, clear air, calm water and intact shore silhouettes remain identical from first to last frame.'",
      "severity": "minor"
    }
